WEBVTT

00:01:39.069 --> 00:01:39.945
I'm sorry.

00:01:40.529 --> 00:01:41.614
But now you know.

00:01:42.531 --> 00:01:44.158
Your body is a fake.

00:01:45.909 --> 00:01:48.162
What do you mean by "fake"?

00:01:49.079 --> 00:01:50.080
What does that mean?

00:01:50.289 --> 00:01:54.960
Your body is made of a special material
called artificial organisms.

00:01:55.753 --> 00:01:58.672
Artificial organisms?

00:01:58.756 --> 00:01:59.673
That's right.

00:02:00.257 --> 00:02:03.093
Hey, now.
Wasn't that a little rough?

00:02:06.305 --> 00:02:07.222
Young lady!

00:02:10.142 --> 00:02:11.060
Heads up!

00:02:16.398 --> 00:02:18.192
That's artificial organisms.

00:02:18.817 --> 00:02:19.818
I know that.

00:02:19.943 --> 00:02:23.197
My dad's company developed
artificial organisms.

00:02:23.822 --> 00:02:25.616
That's right, isn't it, Aiko?

00:02:28.118 --> 00:02:30.162
Remember me? I'm Kurose.

00:02:30.829 --> 00:02:34.166
I worked with your doctors,
Yura and Isazu.

00:02:42.049 --> 00:02:44.343
Mr. Kurose! What is this all about?

00:02:45.177 --> 00:02:46.595
Please, take a seat.

00:02:49.556 --> 00:02:51.725
It's a rather complicated story.

00:02:51.809 --> 00:02:53.936
Try and stay calm while I tell it.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:57.773
Two years ago, in the fall,

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:00.526
you were injured in a car accident.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:05.072
You had to endure
a long hospital stay and rehabilitation.

00:03:06.615 --> 00:03:09.868
However, your injuries
were so severe then,

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:13.831
that we weren't able to save your life.

00:03:15.958 --> 00:03:16.875
What?

00:03:17.668 --> 00:03:19.503
In order to save you,

00:03:19.837 --> 00:03:23.382
we decided to utilize a technology
that we had developed.

00:03:23.924 --> 00:03:27.511
You were the first person
this treatment was ever used on.

00:03:28.095 --> 00:03:30.681
The first person ever?

00:03:30.764 --> 00:03:31.640
That's right.

00:03:31.724 --> 00:03:34.810
We separated your brain from your body

00:03:35.352 --> 00:03:37.688
and treated each separately.

00:03:39.732 --> 00:03:42.192
However, if we simply separated them,

00:03:42.276 --> 00:03:45.237
it'd be impossible to sustain
your body and brain.

00:03:45.612 --> 00:03:50.159
<i>So, we created a duplicate body</i>
<i>using artificial organisms.</i>

00:03:51.285 --> 00:03:53.829
<i>We put your brain into the artificial body</i>

00:03:53.996 --> 00:03:59.209
<i>and the artificial brain into your body</i>
<i>to keep you alive.</i>

00:03:59.835 --> 00:04:04.173
<i>The person named Aiko Tachibana</i>
<i>now has two existences.</i>

00:04:05.424 --> 00:04:07.843
There are two of me?

00:04:08.343 --> 00:04:10.429
When you were born,

00:04:10.763 --> 00:04:14.475
a copy of your body was made
using artificial organisms.

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:16.769
That's your duplicate.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:20.397
What? You mean my clone?

00:04:20.773 --> 00:04:21.857
It's not a clone.

00:04:22.316 --> 00:04:26.820
It's a body exactly like yours
that is made of artificial living cells.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.990
Why was that made?

00:04:30.324 --> 00:04:33.702
Your father's company
and Kiryu Research partnered

00:04:34.161 --> 00:04:36.705
in an experiment to construct

00:04:36.789 --> 00:04:39.333
duplicates of employees
and their families.

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:44.880
You had a checkup at Kiryu Research
every year on your birthday, right?

00:04:47.174 --> 00:04:49.635
<i>That was to compare you to the duplicate</i>

00:04:49.718 --> 00:04:51.845
<i>and confirm it was growing properly.</i>

00:04:52.805 --> 00:04:54.181
What? Are you serious?

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:58.435
Dad never told me that! Nobody did.

00:04:59.228 --> 00:05:00.813
And that surgery!

00:05:00.979 --> 00:05:02.981
Dr. Isazu never said anything!

00:05:03.565 --> 00:05:06.109
It was top secret at Kiryu Research.

00:05:06.318 --> 00:05:09.488
Such information could not be made public.

00:05:10.072 --> 00:05:12.282
But Dad told me

00:05:12.449 --> 00:05:15.035
that even artificial organism technology

00:05:15.118 --> 00:05:17.538
can't create brains or whole bodies!

00:05:17.621 --> 00:05:20.582
Only one person succeeded in doing that.

00:05:23.085 --> 00:05:24.253
Toshihide Yura.

00:05:25.837 --> 00:05:27.798
Dr. Yura?

00:05:33.178 --> 00:05:35.222
Your real body is there.

00:05:37.641 --> 00:05:38.725
At the Gate?

00:05:39.309 --> 00:05:43.438
Yes, it's through that gate,
far into the area beyond it.

00:05:44.022 --> 00:05:46.066
What? At ground zero?

00:05:47.568 --> 00:05:48.485
Correct.

00:05:48.652 --> 00:05:50.821
Ground zero, Primary Point.

00:05:51.863 --> 00:05:55.158
We can get your real body back
if we go there.

00:05:55.784 --> 00:05:59.246
My real body.

00:06:00.455 --> 00:06:02.499
They're still alive there, too...

00:06:03.542 --> 00:06:05.627
your mother and little brother.

00:06:05.794 --> 00:06:06.670
What?

00:06:08.714 --> 00:06:10.549
You might be able to save them.

00:06:11.508 --> 00:06:13.885
How can you possibly know that?

00:06:22.144 --> 00:06:23.312
<i>What is this?</i>

00:06:26.481 --> 00:06:28.567
<i>They wore those clothes that day!</i>

00:06:30.402 --> 00:06:32.279
<i>Their hair is growing.</i>

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:35.032
<i>They've been alive since that day.</i>

00:06:37.409 --> 00:06:39.953
It's up to you to believe it or not.

00:06:40.037 --> 00:06:43.165
But you can only save
your mother and brother

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:46.084
by going to Primary Point.

00:06:48.045 --> 00:06:49.880
I want you to come with us.

00:06:50.464 --> 00:06:54.217
But why would you go
to such a dangerous place

00:06:54.301 --> 00:06:56.720
to help me and my family?

00:06:57.429 --> 00:06:59.723
If you can get your real body back,

00:07:00.223 --> 00:07:02.559
we can put an end to the Burst.

00:07:02.643 --> 00:07:05.437
What? End the Burst?

00:07:07.648 --> 00:07:09.691
<i>Yuya Kanzaki kidnapped Aiko Tachibana?</i>

00:07:09.775 --> 00:07:10.609
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

00:07:11.193 --> 00:07:15.906
The school transfer paperwork
for this Kanzaki guy was forged.

00:07:16.239 --> 00:07:19.868
That person doesn't even exist.

00:07:20.577 --> 00:07:21.828
Where are they now?

00:07:22.412 --> 00:07:23.830
In the Border Zone.

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:26.541
The Town, huh?

00:07:30.796 --> 00:07:31.964
As you know,

00:07:32.547 --> 00:07:36.718
two years ago, the abnormal
artificial cell proliferation occurred

00:07:36.969 --> 00:07:39.304
at Kiryu Biotech Research Facility Two.

00:07:39.721 --> 00:07:41.723
It was known as the Burst.

00:07:42.182 --> 00:07:44.810
The Malignant Matter that caused the Burst

00:07:44.977 --> 00:07:46.520
spilled out of the facility,

00:07:47.104 --> 00:07:49.606
and flowed downriver
through the valley.

00:07:50.524 --> 00:07:53.777
The government immediately
upgraded the dams

00:07:53.986 --> 00:07:56.989
into barriers to prevent the Matter
from advancing.

00:07:57.614 --> 00:08:00.242
However, it overcame each barrier,

00:08:00.367 --> 00:08:03.829
and has now reached
a point just before the Sea of Japan.

00:08:04.746 --> 00:08:08.083
If it gets beyond Aimoto Dam,
the so-called Gate,

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:11.044
<i>it's impossible to imagine</i>
<i>the amount of damage</i>

00:08:11.128 --> 00:08:13.463
<i>it would cause to Japan and the world.</i>

00:08:13.547 --> 00:08:15.257
I already know that!

00:08:15.424 --> 00:08:18.385
The trigger that caused the Burst
was the surgery

00:08:19.136 --> 00:08:21.263
that separated your mind and body.

00:08:23.223 --> 00:08:26.143
My surgery caused it?

00:08:27.394 --> 00:08:28.311
What are you saying?

00:08:31.023 --> 00:08:31.898
You mean

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:35.527
I'm the cause of the Burst?

00:08:35.861 --> 00:08:36.945
Don't worry.

00:08:38.238 --> 00:08:39.239
It wasn't you.

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:41.992
It was the surgery performed on you.

00:08:42.492 --> 00:08:44.578
When your body and brain were separated,

00:08:44.661 --> 00:08:46.997
your duplicate treated it as a crisis.

00:08:47.497 --> 00:08:50.584
It sent other artificial organisms
in the research facility's pool

00:08:50.959 --> 00:08:52.544
into abnormal cell proliferation.

00:08:53.837 --> 00:08:56.298
You expect me to believe that?

00:08:56.882 --> 00:08:58.717
Why are you trying to deceive me?

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:02.179
You used some kind of trick
to turn my cheek black, didn't you?

00:09:02.763 --> 00:09:05.098
That video of Mom and Ryota could be...

00:09:06.016 --> 00:09:07.267
What?

00:09:09.644 --> 00:09:10.604
Watch this.

00:09:21.573 --> 00:09:22.699
Is that writing?

00:09:23.492 --> 00:09:25.994
<i>This is your body's serial number.</i>

00:09:28.163 --> 00:09:29.372
Please believe us.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:33.794
We will do whatever it takes
to end this disaster.

00:09:36.213 --> 00:09:38.340
We need your cooperation.

00:09:39.299 --> 00:09:41.551
I know it is hard to accept this

00:09:41.635 --> 00:09:43.011
just because we ask you to.

00:09:43.095 --> 00:09:45.430
It's gotta be a real shock.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:47.933
Who knew such a thing could happen?

00:09:48.141 --> 00:09:49.726
That's why I hired you.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:52.979
Just like you requested,
I formed a skilled team.

00:09:53.688 --> 00:09:55.398
Do you want to see them?

00:09:56.108 --> 00:09:57.609
-Yuya.
-Yes?

00:09:58.693 --> 00:10:00.654
Are you going to take her along?

00:10:01.113 --> 00:10:03.115
We can't leave her here alone.

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:06.576
Wasn't there an extra pair
of shoes over here?

00:10:06.743 --> 00:10:08.662
I got her shoes.

00:10:09.204 --> 00:10:12.082
What? Then get them out...

00:10:15.168 --> 00:10:16.545
Hey! This is the fifth floor!

00:10:26.138 --> 00:10:28.265
-Damn!
-She's adapted fast!

00:10:29.015 --> 00:10:31.309
Emergency backup needed in the Zone!

00:10:33.478 --> 00:10:36.314
There is really something
strange about me!

00:10:37.524 --> 00:10:38.483
I can move now!

00:10:43.697 --> 00:10:44.823
What was that?

00:10:45.448 --> 00:10:47.868
<i>Special custody subject at large!</i>

00:10:47.951 --> 00:10:49.828
<i>Young girl in school uniform!</i>

00:10:49.911 --> 00:10:51.913
<i>Requesting assistance! I repeat.</i>

00:10:51.997 --> 00:10:53.498
<i>Special custody subject at large!</i>

00:10:53.999 --> 00:10:55.876
<i>Young girl in school uniform!</i>

00:10:57.294 --> 00:10:59.546
Why is this happening to me?

00:11:04.259 --> 00:11:05.760
Special custody subject found!

00:11:10.223 --> 00:11:11.516
Who is that?

00:11:17.105 --> 00:11:18.565
You sneaky bitch!

00:11:19.691 --> 00:11:20.734
What's this about?

00:11:20.817 --> 00:11:22.569
The Hinosawa Pharma lab!

00:11:22.652 --> 00:11:23.570
Never heard of it.

00:11:23.653 --> 00:11:24.529
Bullshit!

00:11:24.613 --> 00:11:26.823
Fine! Like I said...

00:11:26.907 --> 00:11:28.283
Here's your order!

00:11:30.285 --> 00:11:31.703
Thank you for the...

00:11:32.871 --> 00:11:35.248
Buzz off.
I'm trying to eat.

00:11:35.332 --> 00:11:36.541
Why you...

00:11:39.044 --> 00:11:39.920
What the...

00:11:43.632 --> 00:11:44.841
How did she...

00:11:44.925 --> 00:11:45.926
From above?

00:11:46.009 --> 00:11:48.178
-Hey, you...
-Are you okay?

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:52.474
-Are you hurt?
-I'm sorry!

00:11:53.141 --> 00:11:54.225
Where is the exit?

00:11:54.309 --> 00:11:56.686
It's over here.

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:57.979
There's a back door.

00:11:58.063 --> 00:12:00.774
-Thank you!
-Hey, what's wrong?

00:12:01.107 --> 00:12:02.817
Wait! This way!

00:12:04.945 --> 00:12:06.988
This is an emergency. I need your help.

00:12:07.155 --> 00:12:08.198
Shino?

00:12:08.782 --> 00:12:10.951
You're not a Diver, are you?

00:12:11.618 --> 00:12:13.286
Why are you in the Town?

00:12:14.579 --> 00:12:15.997
-Please help me!
-What?

00:12:16.081 --> 00:12:17.958
I want to get out of here!

00:12:18.041 --> 00:12:19.292
In that case,

00:12:19.876 --> 00:12:21.127
go that way.

00:12:25.048 --> 00:12:26.091
There you are.

00:12:27.092 --> 00:12:28.635
-There she is!
-Thank God!

00:12:28.718 --> 00:12:29.803
Calm down, honey.

00:12:29.886 --> 00:12:31.763
What do you think you're doing?

00:12:31.846 --> 00:12:34.182
Don't you dare treat a woman like that!

00:12:35.225 --> 00:12:36.059
Who are you?

00:12:36.142 --> 00:12:37.185
I'll introduce you.

00:12:37.602 --> 00:12:38.436
Huh?

00:12:38.687 --> 00:12:40.313
This is my buddy, Shiraishi.

00:12:41.439 --> 00:12:42.691
Nice to meet you.

00:12:44.526 --> 00:12:46.695
Mission... complete?

00:12:49.155 --> 00:12:51.324
<i>I'm sorry we scared you.</i>

00:12:51.658 --> 00:12:54.953
<i>I know it's hard for you</i>
<i>to accept it all so easily.</i>

00:12:55.704 --> 00:12:59.374
But I want you to understand
that these are not bad people.

00:13:00.041 --> 00:13:02.627
Can we have more time
to explain all this?

00:13:03.128 --> 00:13:04.337
Please! I'm begging!

00:13:07.173 --> 00:13:10.051
You want us to work for you, Shino?

00:13:10.635 --> 00:13:11.761
What is this about?

00:13:11.886 --> 00:13:13.805
I looked you up on the server.

00:13:14.389 --> 00:13:16.099
Both your teams are solid.

00:13:18.018 --> 00:13:19.728
That's our mission log!

00:13:19.811 --> 00:13:21.146
Why do you have that?

00:13:21.646 --> 00:13:24.524
Your agility, judgment, and energy levels

00:13:24.899 --> 00:13:26.776
are all way off the charts.

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:29.696
Coming from you, that means a lot, Shino.

00:13:29.779 --> 00:13:31.114
You have a good eye.

00:13:31.698 --> 00:13:33.158
So, what's the target?

00:13:34.743 --> 00:13:37.746
Kiryu Biotech Research Facility Two.

00:13:38.371 --> 00:13:39.789
Primary Point.

00:13:39.873 --> 00:13:40.832
-What?
-What?

00:13:40.915 --> 00:13:42.083
Ground Zero?

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:46.004
Right. We're going to recover
something important from there.

00:13:46.588 --> 00:13:51.509
To get it, we have to bring the key
that unlocks it to Primary Point.

00:13:51.843 --> 00:13:55.388
No one's ever returned from Area Three,
and this is even deeper.

00:13:55.472 --> 00:13:57.140
Who the hell would go there?

00:13:57.557 --> 00:14:00.602
Don't tell me the key is...

00:14:01.186 --> 00:14:04.314
That girl you captured earlier.

00:14:06.024 --> 00:14:07.359
She's just a civilian!

00:14:07.442 --> 00:14:08.693
She'll never make it!

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:10.820
Who the hell is that girl?

00:14:11.529 --> 00:14:13.406
<i>I can't tell you right now.</i>

00:14:17.494 --> 00:14:18.787
Let's take a break.

00:14:25.377 --> 00:14:28.296
It appears that Cell Assembler Two

00:14:28.505 --> 00:14:31.841
has performed the way I hoped it would.

00:14:32.342 --> 00:14:36.679
As predicted, my body is aging properly.

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:40.642
I can have a very fulfilling death.

00:14:41.309 --> 00:14:43.019
It's quite interesting.

00:14:43.186 --> 00:14:45.897
Although the physical body
moves toward death,

00:14:46.022 --> 00:14:49.567
the mind intends
to continue living forever.

00:14:50.235 --> 00:14:54.656
Cell Assembler Two could make
eternal life possible.

00:14:55.031 --> 00:14:59.285
For the sake of Kiryu Research
and for all of humanity,

00:14:59.869 --> 00:15:02.497
I hope you live for as long as possible.

00:15:03.373 --> 00:15:07.210
The future is created by new lives.

00:15:07.502 --> 00:15:11.840
Artificial organisms have proven
that life can take a new form.

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:15.301
I want you to take over
development from here.

00:15:17.429 --> 00:15:20.181
By the way, how is Yuzuha doing?

00:15:22.267 --> 00:15:25.562
My daughter is still in a coma.

00:15:26.146 --> 00:15:27.063
I see.

00:15:28.523 --> 00:15:30.483
If only Toshi were still here.

00:15:31.067 --> 00:15:34.529
I swear that I'll bring her back
to consciousness.

00:15:35.071 --> 00:15:38.741
Toshihide Yura is
no longer alive after all.

00:15:40.618 --> 00:15:44.706
<i>You all know the Gate well,</i>
<i>also known as Aimoto Dam.</i>

00:15:45.206 --> 00:15:47.333
<i>You'll move through into Area One,</i>

00:15:47.417 --> 00:15:49.544
<i>then bust through K1 into Area Two.</i>

00:15:49.878 --> 00:15:53.715
<i>After gearing up</i>
<i>at Yanagawara Camp in Area Two,</i>

00:15:53.923 --> 00:15:57.844
<i>you'll proceed similarly</i>
<i>through Areas Three, Four and Five</i>

00:15:57.927 --> 00:16:02.599
<i>to arrive at Primary Point,</i>
<i>Kiryu Biotech Research Facility Two.</i>

00:16:03.766 --> 00:16:06.478
We won't be able to destroy
the Matter on this mission

00:16:06.561 --> 00:16:07.687
and won't have to.

00:16:08.396 --> 00:16:11.191
As long as we deliver her
to the target point,

00:16:11.274 --> 00:16:12.484
we'll achieve our goal.

00:16:12.692 --> 00:16:15.612
And we're doing that insanity
with so few people?

00:16:15.945 --> 00:16:16.863
That's right.

00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:21.201
To reach the target point while avoiding
the Matter as it transforms,

00:16:21.326 --> 00:16:24.579
it's best that the team
be as small as possible.

00:16:25.163 --> 00:16:26.498
As small as possible?

00:16:26.748 --> 00:16:28.333
I believe this mission

00:16:28.917 --> 00:16:33.046
will be the most difficult
any of us has ever attempted.

00:16:33.296 --> 00:16:34.130
However,

00:16:34.797 --> 00:16:37.592
I'm certain
you're the ones to pull it off.

00:16:40.261 --> 00:16:42.096
Sure, I'm in!

00:16:42.639 --> 00:16:44.265
It <i>does</i> sound pretty cool.

00:16:44.349 --> 00:16:45.350
You're crazy.

00:16:45.642 --> 00:16:48.811
You get how dangerous it is,
don't you, Kaede?

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:50.355
That's why I'm in.

00:16:51.105 --> 00:16:52.315
Then, I'll go, too.

00:16:53.858 --> 00:16:54.734
Sagami?

00:16:55.193 --> 00:16:56.444
You ready for this?

00:16:57.737 --> 00:17:00.406
We have no idea
what kind of Matter we'll run into.

00:17:04.118 --> 00:17:07.330
So, the Misawa-Seri team is
with us, right?

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:09.207
-You got it.
-Right.

00:17:09.749 --> 00:17:12.168
I've deposited advances
into your accounts.

00:17:15.088 --> 00:17:16.381
-What?
-Wow!

00:17:16.464 --> 00:17:19.759
You'll get a completion bonus
once the job is done.

00:17:20.468 --> 00:17:23.805
I can't guarantee you'll live,
but I <i>can</i> guarantee you'll get paid.

00:17:25.557 --> 00:17:28.977
If we do make it back,
I think we can manage on this.

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:29.978
Kaede!

00:17:30.853 --> 00:17:31.854
I like it!

00:17:32.105 --> 00:17:33.731
You make a tempting offer.

00:17:35.066 --> 00:17:37.443
Fine. We're in.

00:17:38.361 --> 00:17:42.615
No Diver has ever been there.
I want to see it with my own eyes.

00:17:42.949 --> 00:17:43.992
I appreciate it.

00:17:44.576 --> 00:17:46.411
You advances are paid, as well.

00:17:46.494 --> 00:17:48.621
Ah, there's just one thing I forgot.

00:17:49.914 --> 00:17:52.458
Like we said,
the fewer people the better.

00:17:52.792 --> 00:17:55.295
But when we enter Primary Point,

00:17:55.962 --> 00:17:57.213
we take only one team.

00:17:57.297 --> 00:17:58.756
-What?
-Why?

00:17:58.965 --> 00:18:00.300
It's a competition.

00:18:00.925 --> 00:18:03.177
We want to use the best team.

00:18:03.469 --> 00:18:06.306
A competition?
We're risking our lives for this!

00:18:06.889 --> 00:18:09.851
We'll decide based on
performances up to Area Three.

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:13.938
Well, then who gets the completion reward?

00:18:14.522 --> 00:18:16.274
One of your two teams.

00:18:20.111 --> 00:18:21.195
Evidence!

00:18:22.113 --> 00:18:23.573
Alpha 72 Omega!

00:18:23.656 --> 00:18:25.491
-Any update?
-None!

00:18:26.075 --> 00:18:28.995
Then why isn't
the vial cartridge working?

00:18:38.796 --> 00:18:40.465
They're shaped like humans.

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:49.140
The shots are going right through!

00:18:58.858 --> 00:19:00.318
YUYA KANZAKI
FINAL REPORT

00:19:06.491 --> 00:19:08.701
Happy 18th Birthday, Yuzuha!

00:19:58.376 --> 00:19:59.836
We have to evacuate!

00:20:04.674 --> 00:20:07.009
-Okay, you're all set.
-Take off!

00:20:44.297 --> 00:20:45.131
Earlier,

00:20:46.466 --> 00:20:49.761
you showed me a video of Mom and Ryota.

00:20:50.344 --> 00:20:53.181
Was that real?

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:55.016
Yes.

00:20:56.017 --> 00:20:58.978
I always thought it was just a dream.

00:20:59.896 --> 00:21:00.730
So,

00:21:01.189 --> 00:21:04.484
who exactly are you, Yuya Kanzaki?

00:21:06.861 --> 00:21:10.698
Everything you already know about me
is all there is to know.

00:21:13.159 --> 00:21:15.620
I bet you're hungry.
I'll get some food.

00:21:27.048 --> 00:21:29.717
So, who is that boy?

00:21:30.301 --> 00:21:32.553
He's your guide beyond Area Three.

00:21:33.137 --> 00:21:36.516
He's the only person who knows
how to use Aiko Tachibana

00:21:36.599 --> 00:21:38.684
to open the lock she's the key to.

00:21:39.227 --> 00:21:40.478
Aiko Tachibana?

00:21:41.062 --> 00:21:42.688
The girl in the school uniform?

00:21:44.273 --> 00:21:46.567
So, her name is Aiko.

00:21:47.235 --> 00:21:49.862
Are you sure he can protect her?

00:21:50.029 --> 00:21:53.366
You want us to escort him
safely up there, too, right?

00:21:53.699 --> 00:21:54.700
Don't worry.

00:21:55.618 --> 00:21:58.454
I will take you to Ground Zero.

00:21:59.288 --> 00:22:03.459
There is something very important
that I have to do there.

00:22:04.335 --> 00:22:06.254
That'll be a sight to see!

00:22:12.510 --> 00:22:14.095
-What was that?
-Upstairs?

00:22:14.804 --> 00:22:15.721
Tachibana!

00:22:15.972 --> 00:22:17.473
-Backup power!
-No good!

00:22:17.557 --> 00:22:18.683
Open the window!

00:22:18.891 --> 00:22:19.725
Yuya!

00:22:26.816 --> 00:22:28.067
They got her!

00:23:57.948 --> 00:23:59.950
Subtitles by Brian Athey
